Hi,

I am having a strange problem with iptables. We have a router setup
where we need to block certain types of traffic based on a certain
criteria (hotspot scenario...).  All rules in the nat table seem to be
bypassed for ESP traffic.=20

=20

iptables -t nat -j DROP

=20

Will not block ESP traffic.

=20

On the other hand

=20

iptables -t filter -p 50 -j DROP=20

=20

will block ESP traffic.

=20

I am using a redhat 9.0 system. I have also installed freeswan but the
module is not loaded.=20

=20

Is any one having similar kinds of problems? Do you think it is because
of the freeswan patches that get installed?

=20

Any inputs, highly appreciated!

=20

Thanks,

Ashwin

=20

=20


